    "https://lynn.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Maintenance/Engineer-I_R0003693": {
      "title": "Maintenance Engineer I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nSummary: The Maintenance Engineer I position will be responsible for maintaining the general condition of the campus with regards to all aspects of basic electrical, carpentry, plumbing, mechanical and painting tasks. Complete maintenance request work orders from Director of Engineering in a timely manner. Participate in the preventive maintenance program for all building equipment. Complete other special task assigned periodically by the Director of Engineering. This position requires consistent adherence to policies and procedures of the department as outlined in Lynn University standard operating procedures and the engineering department standard operating procedures. Job Description: Essential d uties and r esponsibilities   Perform preventive maintenance on all building common area hardware as scheduled, this requires the individual to visually inspect and detect items needing repair and requires knowledge of a wide variety of maintenance trade.   Receive daily work order assignments from the department head and through the automated work order system.   Respond to maintenance calls and opportunities in a positive and polite manner.   Ensure all mechanical calls are attended to in a timely manner, while still maintaining quality craftmenship.    Make rounds by inspecting assigned areas through digital checklist and note any information needed for concerns in the building s .   Perform hardware work; repair or replacement of, door, lever, blinds, drawers,cylinder, minor carpentry if needed, ect.    Perform minor electrical work orders if needed : replace outlets, reset breakers, replace ballasts,use test equipment: voltage tester, amp meter ect.   Perform minor plumbing work orders: unclog drain lines, repair or replace valves, replace gasket, valves, vacuum breaker.   Think quickly and act appropriate in emergency situation and follow all emergency response procedures.   Ensure jobsite is clean and orderly after the completion of all jobs.   Perform well under pressure situations, time demands, and work overtime as needed and as requested by department head.   Report major repair and safety concerns to the department head or any senior campus leader as applicable.   Required k nowledge, s kills, and a bilities   Basic working knowledge of building maintenance, electrical, plumbing, and HVAC .   Ability to push, pull, grasp lift or carry supplies weighting up to 100 lbs.   Ability to communicate effectively.    A ble to provide communication and directio n.   Able to p erform job function with attention to detail .   A ble to prioritize task functions .   Able to t hink clearly, remain calm and resolve unexpected issues using sound judgment .   Able to f ollow direction thoroughly .   Able to u nderstand guest and residence service needs .   Able to w ork cohesively with co-workers as part of a team .   Able to w ork with minimal supervision .   Able to m aintain confidentiality of residence and building’s informatio n.   Able to a dapt to multitasking .   Able to m ove, lift, carry, push, pull and place objects weighing less than or equal to 100 lbs .   Able to s tand, sit or walk for an extended period of time or for an entire work shift .   Able to reach overhead and below the knees, including bending, twisting, pulling and stopping.   Able to c ommunicate with employee, managers, subordinate, residence and guest through verbal communication, hearing ability, and visual acuity.   Able to a dapt to moderate temperature through the property .   Able to work outdoors for long periods of time.     Minimum q ualification s   High school Diploma or equivalent.   One year of relevant experience.   \n Accreditation and equal opportunity Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, age, pregnancy, parenting status, veteran status or retirement status in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of sex. Inquiries concerning the application of the non-discrimination policy may be directed to the Lynn University Compliance Officer/Title IX Coordinator at 3601 N. Military Trail, Boca Raton, FL 33431, titleixcoordinator@lynn.edu, or +1 561-237-7727; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Lynn University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award baccalaureate, master's and doctoral degrees. Contact the Commission on Colleges at 1866 Southern Lane, Decatur, Georgia 30033-4097 or call +1 404-679-4500 for questions about the accreditation of Lynn University. 2020 Lynn University Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling +1 561-237-7639. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Clery Act, the University annually provides a report to each student and current employee, as well as to prospective employees and students, that provides a detailed disclosure of information regarding campus security practices (including Emergency Response Plan, Timely Warnings, Emergency Warnings, Missing Persons, fire safety policies, fire prevention data, and Crime Log policies), as well as crime and fire-related incident statistics for the preceding year. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at lynn.edu/securityreport For your health, Lynn University is smoke- and tobacco-free."
