    "https://lynn.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Green-Center/Financial-Aid-Counselor_R0004172-1": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nSummary: The Financial Aid Counselor provides and supports the vision and mission of the university and Student Financial Services (SFS) Department by establishing and maintaining the highest level of customer service to Lynn students and parents. The Financial Aid Counselor awards students financial aid, processes the awards and advises the students on all aspects of financial aid and their student account. They will apply and be knowledgeable on all institutional, state and federal regulations. They ensure that they meet the mission and goal of the university. The counselor will participate in special projects and communication/outreach activities. The Financial Aid Counselor will provide accurate information to students and parents in-person or via e-mail, virtual platform and phone. The Financial Aid Counselor will provide high-quality, cross-functional administrative services that supports all SFS team members by promoting and coordinating student-oriented training sessions that focus on retention, recruitment, and are conducive to an overall campus team building environment. The counselor will work closely with the Specialists to ensure the highest quality customer service for students, parents and the Lynn community. Job Description: Essential duties and responsibilities Package and process financial aid for students Advise students and/or parents on financial aid package and SFS-related processes Counselor assists Student Accounts in the management of the accounts receivable with the primary goal of decreasing delinquent accounts and encouraging timely payments Call students that are missing information or documents to expedite processing of their financial aid Assist in special projects as requested by SFS leadership Assist in completion of other counselors’ work during paid time-off or unplanned absences Daily Functions Perform verification Package financial aid Update status of financial aid as needed Update all pertinent loan data prior to origination Review and approve student Refund Request Forms Contact students for missing financial aid forms as needed Contact students that have paid a deposit but have not sent in their ISIR Counsel students and/or parents about financial aid and financing options Answer phone calls concerning financial aid and account balances Consult with Admission, Registrar, Advising and other departments to help resolve student issues and concerns Weekly Functions Recalculate financial aid as needed Review assigned student population to ensure timely disbursement of aid Assist the Financial Aid Committee in reviewing financial aid appeals, Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP), Professional Judgment (PJ) and endowed scholarship applications Semester Functions: Graduated/withdrawal worksheets Assist with the student check-in process (new and continuing students) Adjust loan amounts and dates when returns are required Review pre-disbursement reports and revise award amounts if needed due to a change in the number of credit hours Conduct financial aid informational meetings as requested Participate in graduation send-off events Conduct New Student Financial Planning meetings via Zoom Yearly Functions Assist in yearly audit Assist in outreach communication events geared towards their specific student population Assist in SAP process, to include canceling aid and notifying students Functions as Needed    Assist the SFS Leadership Team Veterans Affairs (VA) certifications Attend seminars, conferences, webinars and other training opportunities Work flex-hours or extra hours during peak periods Assist in completion of other counselors’ work during paid time-off or unplanned absences Assist at SFS front counter Assist in any function in relation to the operation of the SFS Department Assist in ensuring completion of loan entrance and exit counseling requirements Attend/present at Preview Days, Open Houses, Admitted Student Experience (ASE) and other on-campus activities Participate in off-campus financial aid events (FAFSA nights, parent sessions, etc.) Preferred knowledge, skills, and abilities Microsoft Suite, PowerFaids, Jenzabar, Workday, federal regulations pertaining to Title IV aid, Florida state programs Minimum qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university; or one to two years related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience \n Accreditation and equal opportunity Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, age, pregnancy, parenting status, veteran status or retirement status in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of sex. Inquiries concerning the application of the non-discrimination policy may be directed to the Lynn University Compliance Officer/Title IX Coordinator at 3601 N. Military Trail, Boca Raton, FL 33431, titleixcoordinator@lynn.edu, or +1 561-237-7727; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Lynn University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award baccalaureate, master's and doctoral degrees. Contact the Commission on Colleges at 1866 Southern Lane, Decatur, Georgia 30033-4097 or call +1 404-679-4500 for questions about the accreditation of Lynn University. 2020 Lynn University Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling +1 561-237-7639. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Clery Act, the University annually provides a report to each student and current employee, as well as to prospective employees and students, that provides a detailed disclosure of information regarding campus security practices (including Emergency Response Plan, Timely Warnings, Emergency Warnings, Missing Persons, fire safety policies, fire prevention data, and Crime Log policies), as well as crime and fire-related incident statistics for the preceding year. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at lynn.edu/securityreport For your health, Lynn University is smoke- and tobacco-free."
    },
    "https://lynn.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/de-Hoernle-International-Center/Associate-Professor_R0003752-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Violin",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nSummary: The Lynn University Conservatory of Music invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, Assistant/Associate Professor of Violin. The successful candidate will be an accomplished artist-teacher with an established professional profile, collegiate teaching experience, and a demonstrated record of recruiting and developing outstanding undergraduate and graduate violin performance majors for professional careers in music. Responsibilities include individual instruction, chamber music coaching, student recruitment, and active participation in the artistic and academic life of the Conservatory. Job Description: Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate violin performance majors through weekly private lessons. Teach and lead weekly violin studio class. Coach chamber music ensembles. Prepare students for recitals, mock auditions, juries, competitions, graduate school auditions, and professional orchestra auditions. Recruit outstanding violin students through auditions, outreach, masterclasses, and other recruitment activities. Participate in admissions by reviewing applications, evaluating auditions, and interviewing prospective students. Maintain accurate student records, including attendance, grades, jury evaluations, and progress reports. Participate in faculty meetings, committees, auditions, performances, commencement, and other university and Conservatory events. Collaborate with faculty and staff to support the mission and artistic excellence of the Conservatory. Maintain an active professional profile that enhances the reputation of the Conservatory. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities  Demonstrated record of excellence as a performing violinist.  Strong commitment to student mentorship and artistic development.  Demonstrated success recruiting and developing highly talented violin performance majors.  Demonstrated success preparing students for professional orchestra auditions, competitions, and graduate study.  Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills.  Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students.  Experience coaching chamber music.  Experience working in a highly selective conservatory or equivalent professional training environment.  Established professional network within the classical music community.  Proficiency with instructional technology, including learning management systems such as Canvas, Microsoft Office, and virtual teaching platforms.  Appreciation for diverse learning styles and the ability to adapt instructional methods to meet student needs.  Minimum Qualifications  Master's degree in Violin Performance; equivalent professional experience may be considered.  Collegiate-level violin teaching experience required.  Residency Requirements Must be established and maintain local residence in South Florida within reasonable daily commuting distance of Lynn University to fulfill regular in-person teaching and campus responsibilities.  Rank and Salar y Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with the candidate's qualifications, experience, and professional profile.  To Apply   Applications must include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae detailing academic and professional credentials, contact information for at least three references, and copies of all college transcripts. Official transcripts will be required before the successful candidate is approved to teach.  Applications received by November 15, 2026, will receive priority consideration. The position will remain open until filled.  \n To Apply          Completed applications will be reviewed upon receipt for match to potential needs. Only completed applications will be reviewed, which must include a short cover letter, resume or CV with detailed academic credentials, three letters of reference, and copies of all college transcripts. Before an applicant is approved to teach official transcripts will also be required. Accreditation and equal opportunity Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, age, pregnancy, parenting status, veteran status or retirement status in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of sex. Inquiries concerning the application of the non-discrimination policy may be directed to the Lynn University Compliance Officer/Title IX Coordinator at 3601 N. Military Trail, Boca Raton, FL 33431, titleixcoordinator@lynn.edu, or +1 561-237-7727; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Lynn University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award baccalaureate, master's and doctoral degrees. Contact the Commission on Colleges at 1866 Southern Lane, Decatur, Georgia 30033-4097 or call +1 404-679-4500 for questions about the accreditation of Lynn University. 2020 Lynn University Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling +1 561-237-7639. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Clery Act, the University annually provides a report to each student and current employee, as well as to prospective employees and students, that provides a detailed disclosure of information regarding campus security practices (including Emergency Response Plan, Timely Warnings, Emergency Warnings, Missing Persons, fire safety policies, fire prevention data, and Crime Log policies), as well as crime and fire-related incident statistics for the preceding year. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at lynn.edu/securityreport For your health, Lynn University is smoke- and tobacco-free."
    },
    "https://lynn.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Campus-Communication-Center/Campus-Safety-Supervisor_R0004157-1": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nSummary: The primary purpose of the Campus Safety Supervisor is to provide oversight to their assigned Campus Safety Officers and represent Lynn University in daily campus safety operations. Ensure proper campus safety personnel and handle any student, faculty, staff, or guest concerns and issues. To maintain a professional customer service-oriented approach at all times. Job Description: Essential duties and responsibilities Provide direct supervision to a designated shift within the operational structure of the department. Engage in consistent support to staff, visible patrol, and astute observation to promote the physical safety of the campus and the safety of students, employees, and guests on the campus. Ensure adequate response to all matters reported during shift. Actively engage in prevention techniques to promote the safety of the campus and elevate concerns to the appropriate administrator for discussion when appropriate. Ensure that all Lynn University policies and procedures are enforced. Resolve conflict with parents, students, faculty, and staff in a professional, courteous, and respectful manner at all times. Execute training requirements for the Campus Safety staff. Review and approve all Incident Reports generated during shift. Ensure the reports contain the relevant facts for dissemination to the university administration. Plan and schedule shift personnel, approve vacation requests, administer counseling and disciplinary action when necessary, and maintain shift personnel records. Provide leadership and management during urgent situations until administrative personnel is present. Actively engage and participate in assessment and accreditation efforts within the campus safety department. Actively engage in programming for students, faculty, and staff relating to campus safety topics. Act as a First Responder when the university is in a crisis (i.e., hurricanes, fires, floods, etc.). Required knowledge, skills, and abilities Intermediate knowledge of Microsoft Word and Excel and familiarity with CCTV. Leadership, Time Management, Multitasking, and crisis management abilities. Minimum Qualifications Highschool diploma or six months to one-year related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Must have a valid driver’s license, clean driving record, and be permitted to drive in the state of Florida. Must be willing and able to be certified in CPR/AED. \n Accreditation and equal opportunity Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, age, pregnancy, parenting status, veteran status or retirement status in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of sex. Inquiries concerning the application of the non-discrimination policy may be directed to the Lynn University Compliance Officer/Title IX Coordinator at 3601 N. Military Trail, Boca Raton, FL 33431, titleixcoordinator@lynn.edu, or +1 561-237-7727; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Lynn University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award baccalaureate, master's and doctoral degrees. Contact the Commission on Colleges at 1866 Southern Lane, Decatur, Georgia 30033-4097 or call +1 404-679-4500 for questions about the accreditation of Lynn University. 2020 Lynn University Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling +1 561-237-7639. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Clery Act, the University annually provides a report to each student and current employee, as well as to prospective employees and students, that provides a detailed disclosure of information regarding campus security practices (including Emergency Response Plan, Timely Warnings, Emergency Warnings, Missing Persons, fire safety policies, fire prevention data, and Crime Log policies), as well as crime and fire-related incident statistics for the preceding year. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at lynn.edu/securityreport For your health, Lynn University is smoke- and tobacco-free."
    },
    "https://lynn.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/de-Hoernle-Sports-and-Cultural-Center/Assistant-Athletic-Trainer_R0004040-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nSummary: The Assistant Athletic Trainer works under the supervision of the Associate Athletic Director, Student Athlete Services and supervises the care of student athletes competing in Lynn University's athletic programs. This position includes all phases of the prevention, medical coverage, evaluation, treatment and rehabilitation of assigned athletic teams. This also includes administrative duties including, but not limited to: daily medical records, insurance claim reports and any other duties as assigned. Sport assignments will be determined. Employment is a full-time, 10-month position. Job Description: Essential duties and responsibilities Prevention of athletic injuries and illnesses Evaluation of athletic injuries Treatment of athletic injuries Providing counseling and education to student athletes Athletic training administrative duties Provide medical coverage of practices and competitions Recordkeeping and documentation Work with doctors and other allied health professionals to deliver care to student athletes Other duties as assigned Knowledge, skills, and abilities Abide by NCAA and Sunshine State Conference rules and regulations Minimum qualifications Bachelor's degree with experience in collegiate athletics. Master's degree preferred. Current NATABOC certification Florida State Licensure (or eligible) Current CPR/AED and First Aid certification \n Accreditation and equal opportunity Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, age, pregnancy, parenting status, veteran status or retirement status in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Lynn University does not discriminate on the basis of sex. Inquiries concerning the application of the non-discrimination policy may be directed to the Lynn University Compliance Officer/Title IX Coordinator at 3601 N. Military Trail, Boca Raton, FL 33431, titleixcoordinator@lynn.edu, or +1 561-237-7727; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Lynn University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award baccalaureate, master's and doctoral degrees. Contact the Commission on Colleges at 1866 Southern Lane, Decatur, Georgia 30033-4097 or call +1 404-679-4500 for questions about the accreditation of Lynn University. 2020 Lynn University Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling +1 561-237-7639. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Clery Act, the University annually provides a report to each student and current employee, as well as to prospective employees and students, that provides a detailed disclosure of information regarding campus security practices (including Emergency Response Plan, Timely Warnings, Emergency Warnings, Missing Persons, fire safety policies, fire prevention data, and Crime Log policies), as well as crime and fire-related incident statistics for the preceding year. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at lynn.edu/securityreport For your health, Lynn University is smoke- and tobacco-free."
